          "text": "HUNG Shêng 洪昇 (T. 昉思, H. 稗畦), 1646?–1704, dramatist and poet, was a native of Jên-ho (Hangchow), Chekiang. He married a granddaughter of the Grand Secretary, Huang Chi [q. v.], and was a disciple of Wang Shih-chên [q. v.] who dedicated a number of poems to him.",
